<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biebrich Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1700–1750</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Biebrich Palace is a baroque palace on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> at Wiesbaden-Biebrich in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, built in stages in the first half of the 18th century for the princes of Nassau-Idstein and Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usingen">Usingen</a>. From 1744 it was their main residence, and later that of the dukes of Nassau until they moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiesbaden">Wiesbaden</a>'s town palace in 1841.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/biebrich-palace.jpg" alt="Biebrich Palace" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fritz Geller-Grimm · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Biebrich_fg01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
